# AdaptiveDialog Implementation Plan

> **For Claude:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.

**Goal:** Build an `AdaptiveDialog` component that renders as a bottom Sheet (corvu Drawer) on mobile (<768px) and a centered Dialog (Kobalte) on tablet+ (≥768px), using a single unified Dialog-style API.

**Architecture:** The root component uses `createBreakpoints` from `@solid-primitives/media` to reactively detect viewport width, then renders either `<DialogPrimitive.Root>` or corvu `<Drawer>` wrapping the same children. A SolidJS context propagates the current mode (`"dialog" | "sheet"`) to sub-components, which each conditionally render their matching primitive (Kobalte's `DialogPrimitive.Trigger` / corvu's `Drawer.Trigger`, etc.). `props.children` is a lazy getter in SolidJS, so sub-components are always evaluated within the correct primitive's context.

**Tech Stack:** SolidJS, `@solid-primitives/media` (createBreakpoints), `@kobalte/core/dialog`, `@corvu/drawer` (via existing Sheet dependency), Tailwind v4, Vitest + `@solidjs/testing-library`

**Key Breakpoints (from `src/styles/theme.css`):**
- `--breakpoint-sm: 37.5rem` (600px)
- `--breakpoint-lg: 56.25rem` (900px)
- `--breakpoint-xl: 75rem` (1200px)
- **No `md` breakpoint exists in the Tailwind config.** The `md: 768px` cutoff is used only for the AdaptiveDialog mode switch, not as a Tailwind class.

**Primitive Mapping:**

| Adaptive | Tablet ≥768px (Kobalte Dialog) | Mobile <768px (corvu Drawer) |
|---|---|---|
| Root | `DialogPrimitive.Root` | `Drawer` |
| Trigger | `DialogPrimitive.Trigger` | `Drawer.Trigger` |
| Content | `DialogPrimitive.Portal` + `Overlay` + `Content` (centered, X close button) | `Drawer.Portal` + `Drawer.Overlay` + `Drawer.Content` (bottom, drag handle) |
| Header | `<div>` wrapper | `<div>` wrapper (same) |
| Title | `DialogPrimitive.Title` | `Drawer.Label` |
| Description | `DialogPrimitive.Description` | `Drawer.Description` |
| Footer | `<div>` wrapper | `<div>` wrapper (same) |

**Constraints:**
- z-index: both use `z-70` (modal layer per project scale)
- Dialog close button (X) only in dialog mode; Sheet uses swipe-to-dismiss + drag handle
- Must pass through `class` prop on all sub-components for flexibility
- `as` prop support on Trigger for polymorphic rendering (e.g. `as={Button}`)
- No arbitrary Tailwind values — use project tokens (`text-subheading`, `text-body-sm`, `border-2`, `border-border`, `shadow-card`, `duration-standard`, `ease-standard`, etc.)
- Corvu Drawer accepts children as either JSX or `(props) => JSX` render function — we use plain JSX

