2. **How to force ref re-fire on `<Show>` re-mount in SolidJS:** If non-keyed `Show` recycles DOM nodes, what is the correct pattern to run a callback every time a `Show` child becomes visible again? Options: (a) use `<Show keyed>` (not applicable here since we don't control Kobalte's internals), (b) use `createEffect` watching a signal instead of a ref, (c) use `onCleanup`/`onMount` inside the child component. Which is idiomatic for "run side effect when Kobalte TabsContent becomes selected/visible"?

